{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Therefore a man shall leave his father and his mother and cling to his wife, etc.</b> The holy spirit says this to prohibit the forbidden sexual relations to the children of Noah." "<b>and they shall be one flesh.</b> The offspring is formed through both of them, and there their flesh becomes one — this is the language of Rashi. But there is no sense in this, for the beast and the wild animal also become one flesh in their offspring. And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that the beast and the wild animal have no attachment to their females, but the male comes upon whatever female he finds and they go their way. And because of this Scripture said that since the human female was bone of his bones and flesh of his flesh, he clung to her and she was in his bosom like his own flesh, and he desires her to be with him always. And since this was so in man, his nature was established in his descendants, that the males among them would be attached to their wives, leaving their father and their mother and seeing their wives as though they are with them as one flesh. And so: \"for he is our brother, our flesh\" (Genesis 37:27), \"to any close relative of his flesh\" (Leviticus 18:6) — relatives in the family are called \"close flesh.\" And so he leaves the closeness of his father and his mother, and sees his wife as closer to him than they."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:04.597284840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}